.TH _NIME 1 "2026-11" "_nime 1.9.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
_nime \- browse and watch anime from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B _nime
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.br
.B _nime-dl
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIquery\fR]
.PP
Run with no arguments and \fB_nime\fR asks for a search term before showing the
anime list.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B _nime-dl
is the same program with \fB\-\-download\fR already set: the menus and options
are identical, episodes are saved instead of played.
.PP
.B _nime
searches an anime streaming site, lists the episodes, resolves the stream and
hands it to a local player. It scrapes the site, talks to its player directly,
including the encrypted stream payload, which it decrypts with
.BR openssl (1).
.PP
A series that the site splits into one entry per season is put back together:
every season is looked up and their episodes are listed as one run, numbered
straight through, with the season shown in front of each episode number.
.PP
Moving to the next or previous episode loads it into the player window that is
already open, and leaving the menu closes that window. This needs
.BR python3 (1)
for the control socket; without it every episode opens its own window.
.PP
When no player is available it prints the stream url, the subtitle url and the
required referer instead of failing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-continue
Continue watching from history.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-download
Download the episode instead of playing it, with
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
or
.BR ffmpeg (1).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-delete
Delete the history file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-episode " \fIn\fR"
Play episode \fIn\fR, or a range such as \fI1\-3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-range " \fIn\fR"
Same as \fB\-\-episode\fR.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " \fIq\fR"
Quality to pick: \fIbest\fR (default), \fIworst\fR, or a height such as
\fI1080\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-select\-nth " \fIn\fR"
Select the nth search result or history entry without opening a menu.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vlc
Use VLC instead of mpv.
.TP
.B \-\-dub
Play the dubbed version. This is the default; use \fB\-\-sub\fR to override
it. When the source it picked has no dub for a show, the other one is checked
and used if it has the dub.
.TP
.BR \-engdub
English dub, the same as \fB\-\-dub\fR.
.TP
.BR \-gerdub ", " \-spadub ", " \-fredub ", " \-itadub ", " \-pordub ", " \-rusdub ", " \-aradub
Request that language's dub. Only English dubs are available from the supported
sources, so these stop with an explanation rather than play the wrong audio.
.TP
.BR \-engsub ", " \-gersub ", " \-fresub ", " \-spasub ", " \-itasub ", " \-porsub ", " \-rusub ", " \-arasub
Subtitles in that language, short for \fB\-\-sub\-lang\fR.
.TP
.BR \-allsub
Every subtitle track, short for \fB\-\-sub\-lang all\fR.
.TP
.BR \-subs ", " \-\-subs
Show subtitles. They stay off otherwise, and the video plays clean.
.TP
.BR \-\-sub\-lang " \fIlang\fR"
Subtitle track to use, as a language code (\fIeng\fR, \fIger\fR, \fIspa\fR) or
as a name (\fIgerman\fR), which also turns subtitles on. With \fB\-\-download\fR,
\fIall\fR embeds every track the source offers. Without it the track the source
marks default is used.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-subs
Print the subtitle tracks available for the selected episode, with language
codes, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-sub
Play the subtitled version instead of the dubbed one.
.TP
.B \-\-skip
Skip the opening and the ending. Works by writing a small mpv script with the
intro and outro marks the player reports. mpv only.
.TP
.B \-\-syncplay
Play through Syncplay, so playback can be shared with other people.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-detach
Keep the player in the foreground instead of backgrounding it.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-deps
Print the state of every required and optional dependency, the detected
player and the default source, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-update
Fetch the script from the git repository, compare versions and replace the
installed copy, keeping the previous one as \fI_nime.bak\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B _NIME_MODE
\fIsub\fR or \fIdub\fR.
.TP
.B _NIME_QUALITY
Default quality.
.TP
.B _NIME_PLAYER
Player command to use instead of the detected one.
.TP
.B _NIME_PLAYER_FLAGS
Extra flags handed to the player.
.TP
.B _NIME_MENU
\fIfzf\fR (default) or \fInone\fR for a numbered prompt.
.TP
.B _NIME_HIST_DIR
Directory holding the history file. Defaults to
\fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/_nime\fR.
.TP
.B _NIME_DOWNLOAD_DIR
The downloads folder itself. Defaults to the XDG download dir, \fI~/Downloads\fR,
\fI~/Desktop\fR or the home directory, whichever exists first. Files are written
to \fI_nime downloads/<series>/\fR inside it.
.TP
.B _NIME_SKIP
Set to \fI1\fR to always skip intros and outros.
.TP
.B _NIME_SUB_LANG
Default subtitle language.
.TP
.B _NIME_COLOR
Set to \fI0\fR to disable colours.
.TP
.B _NIME_USER ", " _NIME_BRANCH
Repository and branch used by \fB\-U\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/_nime/nime-hsts
History: one tab separated line per anime, holding the episode, the source, the
id and the title.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/_nime/nime-skip.lua
Generated mpv script used by \fB\-\-skip\fR.
.TP
.I <download folder>/_nime downloads/<series>/
Where \fB\-\-download\fR writes, one folder per series, files named
\fIE<episode>.mp4\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Search and play interactively:
.EX
_nime "<title>"
.EE
.TP
Play episode five in 1080p:
.EX
_nime \-q 1080 \-e 5 "<title>"
.EE
.TP
Watch the other source with intros skipped:
.EX
_nime \-\-skip \-s 2 "<title>"
.EE
.TP
Continue from history:
.EX
_nime \-c
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error, including a failed search, a missing player, a
failed decryption or an episode that could not be resolved.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR openssl (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR vlc (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
